530 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 104 0 R/T(Time: both are O\(L\) per entry, where L is the length of the text. The string approach scans the text several times \(replace, isdigit, ...\) so it has a larger constant; try/except is a single pass and is the more Pythonic \('easier to ask forgiveness than permission'\). In the final design I use try/except and then range validation.)/E(Time: both are O\(L\) per entry, where L is the length of the text. The string approach scans the text several times \(replace, isdigit, ...\) so it has a larger constant; try/except is a single pass and is the more Pythonic \('easier to ask forgiveness than permission'\). In the final design I use try/except and then range validation.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

