<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 111 0 R/T(Manual testing: the tester types each input, reads the output and compares it by eye.Automated testing: a function holds the cases and usesassert actual == expected; the whole suite runs with one command and fails loudly at the first wrong result. After a change \(for example a rate revision\), manual testing must be repeated from scratch - effort proportional to the number of cases T, every time, and error-prone - while automated testing costs the same one command and a few milliseconds of machine time \(O\(T\)\). For this reason I rerun test_calculator.py after every change. \(Larger projects use unittest or pytest, which also report all failures.\))/E(Manual testing: the tester types each input, reads the output and compares it by eye.Automated testing: a function holds the cases and usesassert actual == expected; the whole suite runs with one command and fails loudly at the first wrong result. After a change \(for example a rate revision\), manual testing must be repeated from scratch - effort proportional to the number of cases T, every time, and error-prone - while automated testing costs the same one command and a few milliseconds of machine time \(O\(T\)\). For this reason I rerun test_calculator.py after every change. \(Larger projects use unittest or pytest, which also report all failures.\))/Pg 24 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

