1010 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 112 0 R/T(2.98 for 6,000 and Rs 74.79 for 150,000. A bank transfers each farmer an amount in whole paise, so the amount that actually leaves the account is the sum of the individually rounded payments. Rounding only the final total gives a figure that no set of real payments adds up to. Therefore the correct bank amount is obtained by rounding each payment.)/E(2.98 for 6,000 and Rs 74.79 for 150,000. A bank transfers each farmer an amount in whole paise, so the amount that actually leaves the account is the sum of the individually rounded payments. Rounding only the final total gives a figure that no set of real payments adds up to. Therefore the correct bank amount is obtained by rounding each payment.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[52]>>
endobj

