<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 114 0 R/T(Worked example: fat 4.35 gives raw steps 8.499999999999996, so round gives 8 steps \(rate 33.20\), while fat 4.45 gives 10 steps \(rate 34.00\) - a 0.10 increase in fat changes the rate by Rs 0.80, and 4.25 and 4.35 both pay 33.20. The exact pro-rata value is 33.00, 33.40 and 33.80 for 4.25, 4.35 and 4.45. With 600 litres, such an error is about Rs 120 for one farmer.)/E(Worked example: fat 4.35 gives raw steps 8.499999999999996, so round gives 8 steps \(rate 33.20\), while fat 4.45 gives 10 steps \(rate 34.00\) - a 0.10 increase in fat changes the rate by Rs 0.80, and 4.25 and 4.35 both pay 33.20. The exact pro-rata value is 33.00, 33.40 and 33.80 for 4.25, 4.35 and 4.45. With 600 litres, such an error is about Rs 120 for one farmer.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[16]>>
