<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 114 0 R/T(round\(\) then has to choose between 7 and 8, so readings 0.05 apart can pay the same, and halves are rounded to even \(7.5 gives 8 but 8.5 gives 8\). Floating-point noise makes it worse. The fix is to use exact Decimal arithmetic and let the step count be fractional \(pro-rata\).)/E(round\(\) then has to choose between 7 and 8, so readings 0.05 apart can pay the same, and halves are rounded to even \(7.5 gives 8 but 8.5 gives 8\). Floating-point noise makes it worse. The fix is to use exact Decimal arithmetic and let the step count be fractional \(pro-rata\).)/Pg 27 0 R/K[25]>>
endobj

