<</Title(round\(\) then has to choose between 7 and 8, so readings 0.05 apart can pay the same, and halves are rounded to even \(7.5 gives 8 but 8.5 gives 8\). Floating-point noise makes it worse. The fix is to use exact Decimal arithmetic and let the step count be fractional \(pro-rata\).)/Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1995 0 R/Prev 2036 0 R>>
