2143 0 obj
<</Title(float vs Decimal: the totals agree to the paise in this experiment, but float carries a tiny binary error \(as in Task 2, where 1,003 additions drifted to 33400.30000000061\) with no guarantee; Decimal is exact. Decimal is roughly 5 to 10 times slower in summing but still only milliseconds for 150,000 payments.)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2008 0 R/Prev 2100 0 R/Next 2188 0 R>>
endobj

2144 0 obj
<</Title(2.98 for 6,000 and Rs 74.79 for 150,000. A bank transfers each farmer an amount in whole paise, so the amount that actually leaves the account is the sum of the individually rounded payments. Rounding only the final total gives a figure that no set of real payments adds up to. Therefore the correct bank amount is obtained by rounding each payment.)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2008 0 R/Prev 2188 0 R/Next 2101 0 R>>
endobj

